{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgAp5UKmaiQfNTjJiBK4j","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Googlebot can't load the note content, so your note pages render as \"NOT FOUND\" for it. I've made the fixes in the repo, but nothing is deployed. I haven't re-run the live test, so the fix is untested against Search Console.\n\n**Cause:** each note page is an empty shell, and `site/app.js` fetches the note from `/v1/notes/<slug>` in the browser. On 2026-09-07 `Disallow: /v1/` was added to `robots.txt`. Googlebot's renderer obeys robots.txt for those fetches too, so the API call is blocked. `app.js` then falls into its error branch and draws \"NOT FOUND\", while the server still returns HTTP 200. That combination is a soft 404. The URL inspection shows exactly this: the page fetch succeeds, but the rendered text says \"NOT FOUND\". Browsers and curl ignore robots.txt, which is why the pages look fine to you.\n\n**Timeline:** the pages crawled in August, before the change, are still indexed. Every note crawled after Sep 7 is a soft 404, which fits the index count falling from 25 to 21.\n\n**Fixes:**\n- **`site/robots.txt`:** I added `Allow: /v1/notes`. The longer match beats `Disallow: /v1/`, so the public read endpoints are crawlable again.\n- **`site/app.js`:** the error state now adds a `noindex` robots meta tag, so a failed load can't be indexed as a page.\n\nAfter you deploy, validate the fix in Search Console and re-run the live URL test. The cause, the fix and a longer-term suggestion (server-side rendering and a real 404 status for unknown slugs) are in `ANSWER.md`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1368,"cache_read_input_tokens":22777,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1368},"output_tokens":563,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"s